---
/**
 * Local-First School Attendance Management System Case Study Page
 * File: src/pages/portfolio/attendance-management-system-school/index.astro
 * Purpose: Detailed case study highlighting the ESP32, RFID, SQLite, and Express.js local-first architecture.
 * Contains: Project summary, architectural pillars, database schema definitions, and visual flow.
 * System Role: Demonstrates hardware/software system design, local network robustness, and security.
 */
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'Local-First IoT Attendance Management System Case Study | Jun Alvior';
const description = 'Local-first school attendance management system utilizing an ESP32 microchip, RC522 RFID reader, OLED screen, Express.js backend, and a better-sqlite3 database.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <main id="main-content" class="flex-grow flex flex-col">
    <!-- ORGANISMS: Project Case Study -->
    <article class="py-24 bg-grey-light dark:bg-[#1a1a1a] flex-grow transition-colors duration-300">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <!-- Breadcrumb -->
        <div class="mb-8 text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
          <a
            href="/quick-portfolio/portfolio/"
            class="hover:text-wood-accent transition-colors flex items-center gap-1 font-medium"
          >
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
            </svg>
            Back to Portfolio
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Header -->
        <header class="mb-12" data-aos="fade-up">
          <div class="mb-8 rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 shadow-xl overflow-hidden aspect-video relative group">
            <img 
              src="/quick-portfolio/assets/school-attendance-system/prototype.jpg" 
              alt="ESP32 IoT Attendance System Breadboard Hardware Prototype" 
              class="w-full h-full object-cover transform group-hover:scale-102 transition-transform duration-700" 
              loading="eager"
            />
            <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-black/90 via-black/30 to-transparent flex flex-col justify-end p-6 md:p-8">
              <h3 class="text-lg md:text-xl font-extrabold text-white mb-1">
                Hardware Breadboard Assembly Prototype
              </h3>
              <p class="text-xs md:text-sm text-gray-300">
                ESP32 NodeMCU connected to RC522 RFID reader, SSD1306 OLED screen, and Active buzzer modules.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4">
            <span class="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-green-100 dark:bg-green-950/50 text-green-700 dark:text-green-400">
              Active Project
            </span>
            <span class="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold bg-wood-100 dark:bg-wood-950/50 text-wood-900 dark:text-wood-100">
              Case Study
            </span>
          </div>
          
          <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight mb-4">
            Local-First School Attendance Management System
          </h1>
          <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed font-normal">
            Zero-Cloud Latency, Tamper-Proof Local Auditing, and Real-Time Hardware Tapping Indicators
          </p>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2.5 mt-6">
            <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-wood-900 dark:text-wood-100 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide shadow-sm">
              ESP32 (C/C++)
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-wood-900 dark:text-wood-100 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide shadow-sm">
              Express.js
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-wood-900 dark:text-wood-100 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide shadow-sm">
              Better-SQLite3
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-wood-900 dark:text-wood-100 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide shadow-sm">
              OLED & Buzzers
            </span>
            <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-wood-900 dark:text-wood-100 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide shadow-sm">
              JWT Security
            </span>
          </div>
        </header>

        <!-- Project Links -->
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mb-16" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="50">
          <a
            href="https://github.com/property360-2/attendance-management-system-school"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="px-6 py-3.5 bg-wood-accent hover:bg-wood-700 text-white font-semibold rounded-xl shadow-md hover:shadow-lg transition-all transform hover:-translate-y-0.5 flex items-center gap-2"
          >
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M12 2C6.477 2 2 6.477 2 12c0 4.42 2.865 8.166 6.839 9.489.5.092.682-.217.682-.482 0-.237-.008-.866-.013-1.7-2.782.603-3.369-1.34-3.369-1.34-.454-1.156-1.11-1.462-1.11-1.462-.908-.62.069-.608.069-.608 1.003.07 1.531 1.03 1.531 1.03.892 1.529 2.341 1.087 2.91.831.092-.646.35-1.086.636-1.336-2.22-.253-4.555-1.11-4.555-4.943 0-1.091.39-1.984 1.029-2.683-.103-.253-.446-1.27.098-2.647 0 0 .84-.269 2.75 1.025A9.564 9.564 0 0112 6.844c.85.004 1.705.115 2.504.337 1.909-1.294 2.747-1.025 2.747-1.025.546 1.377.203 2.394.1 2.647.64.699 1.028 1.592 1.028 2.683 0 3.842-2.339 4.687-4.566 4.935.359.309.678.919.678 1.852 0 1.336-.012 2.415-.012 2.743 0 .267.18.579.688.481C19.137 20.164 22 16.418 22 12c0-5.523-4.477-10-10-10z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
            </svg>
            View Code Repository
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Content Flow -->
        <div class="space-y-16">
          
          <!-- Executive Summary -->
          <section id="executive-summary" class="bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] border-l-4 border-wood-accent border-y border-r border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 rounded-r-2xl p-6 sm:p-8" data-aos="fade-up">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-wood-accent shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12h6m-6 4h6m2 5H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z" />
              </svg>
              Executive Summary
            </h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
              The <strong>Local-First School Attendance Management System</strong> is a highly optimized hardware-to-software ecosystem designed for schools and institutions facing frequent internet drops. By utilizing a local-first architecture, the ESP32 scanner communicates directly with a local Express.js REST server hosting a fast, high-performance SQLite database.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mt-3">
              The system features secure user validation, real-time hardware status cues via an **SSD1306 OLED screen** and **Active Buzzer**, and JWT authenticated admin endpoints, providing a bulletproof, <strong>zero-cloud operational model</strong> that stays 100% functional during WAN outages.
            </p>
          </section>

          <!-- System Demonstration Videos -->
          <section id="system-demo" class="space-y-6" data-aos="fade-up">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 pb-3">
              System Demonstration & Walkthrough
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm">
              Watch the physical hardware scanner validation, screen/audio cue triggers, and local-first database checks in action:
            </p>
            
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
              <!-- Walkthrough Video 1 -->
              <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
                <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-black aspect-video relative">
                  <video 
                    src="/quick-portfolio/assets/school-attendance-system/Simple_Attendance_System_School.mp4" 
                    controls 
                    class="w-full h-full object-cover" 
                    preload="metadata"
                  >
                    Your browser does not support the video tag.
                  </video>
                </div>
                <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-300 font-medium text-center">
                  Walkthrough 1: System overview, card scanning flow, and software interface.
                </span>
              </div>

              <!-- Walkthrough Video 2 -->
              <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
                <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 bg-black aspect-video relative">
                  <video 
                    src="/quick-portfolio/assets/school-attendance-system/6fa1635f-60a2-48f9-bf86-854dc9e1ff2e.mp4" 
                    controls 
                    class="w-full h-full object-cover" 
                    preload="metadata"
                  >
                    Your browser does not support the video tag.
                  </video>
                </div>
                <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-300 font-medium text-center">
                  Walkthrough 2: RFID scan detection speed, real-time OLED alerts, and buzzer feedback validation.
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- System Layout Details -->
          <section id="system-details" class="space-y-6" data-aos="fade-up">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 pb-3">
              Hardware Connection Specifications
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm">
              The microcontroller interfaces directly with three peripherals using SPI and I2C buses. Below is the exact electrical mapping:
            </p>
            
            <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 mt-4">
              <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] text-sm">
                <thead>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-[#1a1a1a] border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">
                    <th class="px-6 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-zinc-200">Device</th>
                    <th class="px-6 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-zinc-200">Peripherals Pins</th>
                    <th class="px-6 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-zinc-200">ESP32 GPIO Pin</th>
                    <th class="px-6 py-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-zinc-200">Protocol / Purpose</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100 dark:divide-gray-800 text-xs font-mono">
                  <tr>
                    <td class="px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white font-sans">RFID Reader (RC522)</td>
                    <td class="px-6 py-3">SDA, SCK, MOSI, MISO, RST</td>
                    <td class="px-6 py-3">GPIO 5, 18, 23, 19, 4</td>
                    <td class="px-6 py-3">SPI Communication</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td class="px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white font-sans">OLED Display (SSD1306)</td>
                    <td class="px-6 py-3">SDA, SCL</td>
                    <td class="px-6 py-3">GPIO 21, 22</td>
                    <td class="px-6 py-3">I2C Communication</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td class="px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white font-sans">Active Buzzer</td>
                    <td class="px-6 py-3">S/IN (Signal)</td>
                    <td class="px-6 py-3">GPIO 15</td>
                    <td class="px-6 py-3">PWM Audio Feedback Cues</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- Core Subsystems -->
          <section id="subsystems" class="space-y-6" data-aos="fade-up">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 pb-3">
              Engineering Architecture Pillars
            </h3>
            
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
              <!-- Pillar 1 -->
              <div class="border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 rounded-xl p-6 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] shadow-sm">
                <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white text-base mb-2">1. Local-First SQLite Database Engine</h4>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
                  Utilizes <code>better-sqlite3</code> for sub-millisecond database queries. By keeping the database file local to the host PC or Raspberry Pi server, the system has zero dependency on cloud databases or external APIs. Scans are logged instantly and safely stored in structured SQLite tables, ready for immediate audit access.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- Pillar 2 -->
              <div class="border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 rounded-xl p-6 bg-white dark:bg-[#252528] shadow-sm">
                <h4 class="font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white text-base mb-2">2. Hardware-Level Feedback Controls</h4>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
                  The ESP32 firmware manages active, non-blocking hardware indicators. When an intern taps their card:
                  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1 text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
                    <li>The OLED display shows custom user profiles and validation feedback.</li>
                    <li>The active buzzer generates distinct frequency pulses (short beeps for success, long pulses for invalid cards).</li>
                  </ul>
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <!-- Conversion CTA Block -->
          <section class="py-12 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-[#252528] rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-800 p-8 text-center my-12" data-aos="fade-up">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4">Interested in integrating offline-first IoT systems?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6 max-w-xl mx-auto">Let's connect to design secure, localized microcontroller endpoints and low-latency database systems.</p>
            <a href="/quick-portfolio/contact/" class="inline-flex items-center px-6 py-3 bg-wood-accent hover:bg-wood-700 text-white font-bold rounded-xl transition-all shadow-md">
              Get in Touch &rarr;
            </a>
          </section>

        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
